stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> NewGame
    NewGame --> NewRound

    NewRound --> TurnStart : deal hands, InitialGlance x2 per player

    %% ===== TURN =====
    TurnStart --> Drawing

    Drawing --> CardDrawn_Deck : CardDrawn - source deck
    Drawing --> CardDrawn_DiscardTop : CardDrawn - source discard pile

    CardDrawn_Deck --> ActionTaken_DiscardImmediate : ActionTaken - discard immediate
    CardDrawn_Deck --> ActionTaken_Swap : ActionTaken - swap

    CardDrawn_DiscardTop --> ActionTaken_Swap : ActionTaken - swap
    CardDrawn_DiscardTop --> ActionTaken_PassBack : ActionTaken - pass back

    %% ---- Power sub-flow ----
    ActionTaken_DiscardImmediate --> RankCheck
    RankCheck --> SpellInvocationDecision : rank is 7 8 9 10 J or Q
    RankCheck --> PowerFlowExit : any other rank, no power possible

    SpellInvocationDecision --> PowerFlowExit : declined
    SpellInvocationDecision --> SpellRevealed : invoked - Glance Spy or Decree
    SpellInvocationDecision --> SpellSwapDecision_Smuggle : invoked - Smuggle, no reveal step

    SpellRevealed --> PowerFlowExit : Glance or Spy, terminal
    SpellRevealed --> SpellSwapDecision_Decree : Decree only

    SpellSwapDecision_Decree --> PowerFlowExit : decision swap or none
    SpellSwapDecision_Smuggle --> PowerFlowExit : swap always executes once invoked

    PowerFlowExit --> QuickDiscardWindow
    ActionTaken_Swap --> QuickDiscardWindow
    ActionTaken_PassBack --> QuickDiscardWindow

    QuickDiscardWindow --> EmptyHandCheck : any player, any time, zero or more QuickDiscardPlayed

    EmptyHandCheck --> RoundOver_EmptyHand : HandEmptied fired, a hand reached zero cards
    EmptyHandCheck --> TrialCallWindow : otherwise

    %% ===== TRIAL =====
    TrialCallWindow --> CW_Resolve : every player logs TestimonyGiven-first or TestimonyWindowPassed
    CW_Resolve --> MatchWindow

    MatchWindow --> MW_Resolve : every non caller logs TestimonyGiven-cross or TestimonyWindowPassed-cross

    MW_Resolve --> NextPlayer : zero Testimony given, not last turn, loop
    MW_Resolve --> ForcedEnd_NoTestimony : zero Testimony given, this was the last turn
    MW_Resolve --> Verdict : one or more Testimony given

    Verdict --> DuelWindow : VerdictResolved, two or more truly eligible Testimony givers remain
    Verdict --> FinalPleaWindow : VerdictResolved, otherwise

    DuelWindow --> DW_Resolve : remaining callers log ChallengeGiven or ChallengeWindowPassed, no action for non testimony givers
    DW_Resolve --> FinalPleaWindow : DuelResolved, real duel if challenged, else plain agreement

    FinalPleaWindow --> ScoringTrial : every player who never gave Testimony and was not removed for Perjury logs PleaTaken or PleaWindowPassed

    NextPlayer --> TurnStart

    ScoringTrial --> UpdateScores
    RoundOver_EmptyHand --> UpdateScores : everyone scored as true bystander
    ForcedEnd_NoTestimony --> UpdateScores : everyone scored as true bystander

    UpdateScores --> RenaissanceCheck
    RenaissanceCheck --> CheckGameOver

    CheckGameOver --> NewRound : all scores under 120
    CheckGameOver --> GameOver : any score 120 or higher, hard wall

    GameOver --> [*]

    note right of RankCheck
        Every discarded card that could carry a
        power gets an explicit SpellInvocationDecision
        event even if declined, no silent skips.
    end note

    note right of Verdict
        Checks first window callers only.
        A false first window caller commits Perjury,
        capped plus true hand sum, stacked.
        Removed from rest of Trial, does not
        affect anyone else.
    end note

    note right of DuelWindow
        Appears only if true eligible count is two or more.
        Gate is on true count, not public count, intentional.
        False cross testimony players still get a Challenge
        button but it resolves as a no op. They already gave
        Testimony so they never reach FinalPleaWindow, they
        default straight to the flat false cross testimony
        penalty regardless of anything else here.
    end note

    note right of FinalPleaWindow
        The single point in the Trial where Plea is offered.
        Only for players who never gave Testimony, first or
        cross, and were not removed for Perjury. Opens after
        Verdict and any Duel have fully resolved, so Perjury
        results and Duel outcome are already public knowledge
        by the time this choice is made. This is also the
        exact mechanism behind the true bystander plus
        Perjury occurred outcome in rules.md, it is the same
        Plea or Decline decision, not a separate event type.
    end note

    note right of RenaissanceCheck
        Only a genuine, non zero, non penalized addition
        landing exactly on 50 or 100 triggers a reset.
        Perjury, Plea, false cross testimony, and Duel loss
        are always blocked. A zero result never retriggers it.
    end note
